summary:
  The distance to the writer is not taken off where the single file is opened.

history:
  Measured 2026-11-12 on a Matroska buffer: 14 s of play, a pause of four,
  Play. The reader was opened at the park, 7.8 s behind the writer, met the
  file's unfinished end four times in 21 s and was reopened each time with
  about a second heard twice. Opened twelve seconds behind, the distance
  the sliding buffer keeps, it plays on without a break.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftLogic.js

find:
  Math.min(place, capturedMs - gapMs)

replace:
  Math.min(place, capturedMs)

expect:
  Killed by tst_timeshiftlogic::test_the_single_file_is_opened_a_safe_distance_behind_its_writer.
  Line-neutral.
